PE 849: Race to Strength / 力量竞赛

=== Problem Description ===
Two competitors race to reach a target strength level.
In each round, each player gains strength according to
some probabilistic rule. The first to reach the target wins.
Compute the expected outcome / probability summed over
many starting configurations.

=== Gambler's Ruin (Classic Model) ===
Two players with initial strengths (a, b).
Fair coin (p=1/2):
  P(A wins | a=1, b=1) = 0.5000
  P(A wins | a=1, b=2) = 0.3333
  P(A wins | a=1, b=3) = 0.2500
  P(A wins | a=1, b=4) = 0.2000
  P(A wins | a=1, b=5) = 0.1667
  P(A wins | a=2, b=1) = 0.6667
  P(A wins | a=2, b=2) = 0.5000
  P(A wins | a=2, b=3) = 0.4000
  P(A wins | a=2, b=4) = 0.3333
  P(A wins | a=2, b=5) = 0.2857
  P(A wins | a=3, b=1) = 0.7500
  P(A wins | a=3, b=2) = 0.6000
  P(A wins | a=3, b=3) = 0.5000
  P(A wins | a=3, b=4) = 0.4286
  P(A wins | a=3, b=5) = 0.3750
  P(A wins | a=4, b=1) = 0.8000
  P(A wins | a=4, b=2) = 0.6667
  P(A wins | a=4, b=3) = 0.5714
  P(A wins | a=4, b=4) = 0.5000
  P(A wins | a=4, b=5) = 0.4444
  P(A wins | a=5, b=1) = 0.8333
  P(A wins | a=5, b=2) = 0.7143
  P(A wins | a=5, b=3) = 0.6250
  P(A wins | a=5, b=4) = 0.5556
  P(A wins | a=5, b=5) = 0.5000

